Package: MethylTraits
Type: Package
Title: Discover and Predict Traits from Whole-Genome
        Methylation/Bisulfite Sequencing Methylation Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Andy", "Madrid", email = "andyamadrid@tyckolab.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A toolkit for whole-genome bisulfite sequencing (WGBS) data stored as bsseq
    objects, covering two complementary tasks. First, discovery and annotation of
    regulatory methylation features: imprinting control regions (ICRs) and stochastic
    epigenetic mutations (SEMs), including gene-level burden association testing and
    GO/KEGG enrichment. Second, prediction of sample-level traits directly from
    methylation: genetic sex (including sex-chromosome aneuploidies such as Turner,
    Klinefelter, triple X, and XYY), self-reported race/ethnicity, PASC (long-COVID)
    status (under develoment), and epigenetic age via a two-tier ensemble stack (a pure-WGBS model and a
    hybrid model incorporating published clocks). Also includes a utility to emulate
    450K/EPICv1/EPICv2 microarray data from WGBS, for cross-platform work and for
    applying the full methylCIPHER clock panel and DunedinPACE.
License: GPL-3
